    layer applies had to read the whole book. Per the OI-6 ruling (log.md
    2026-07-13): budget + index now; the doc split is deferred until size forces it.
    
    (1) Applies-when index: a 22-row table at the top of PROCESS_OPTIONS.md, one
    row per `##` layer in document order - Layer | Applies when (skip the section
    if not) | What it adds - so the common path is scan one table, read one section.
    
    (2) Byte budget (watched, the PROCESS.md model - not a hard test, which would
    fight legitimate additions to a doc holding every opt-in layer): registered
    PROCESS_OPTIONS.md in the byte-budget-guard skill with baseline 134,965,
    reworded the intro + expansion-homes note, extended the wc command; synced the
    2 agent copies (bootstrap --sync) and regenerated skills/INDEX.csv. A Byte
    budget note in the doc points at the skill and records the deferred split.
    
    Byte delta (flagged): PROCESS_OPTIONS.md 130,964 -> 134,965 (+4,001 = the index
    table; establishes the watched baseline). AGENTS.template.md/PROCESS.md
    unchanged. Commit bar: smoke 563 passed/2 skipped, check_docs --stale exit 0,
    skills-sync 10/10.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

